        "reference": "Alma 49:25",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 49,
        "verse": 25
      },
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass that he was exceedingly angry with his people, because he had not obtained his desire over the Nephites; he had not subjected them to the yoke of bondage.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 26,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 49:26",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 49,
        "verse": 26
      },
      {
        "text": "Yea, he was exceedingly wroth, and he did curse God, and also Moroni, swearing with an oath that he would drink his blood; and this because Moroni had kept the commandments of God in preparing for the safety of his people.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
